{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>I gathered</b>. I assembled, like <i>for you, gather all the Jews</i>." "<b>And the word סגולה</b>. A coveted thing, kept to boast in, like the precious stones found among kings, and coveted things found in one city alone." "<b>And the matter of שדה ושדות</b>. They are the women, and <i>and the delights of the sons of men</i> indicates it; and furthermore, he mentioned all the desires of the world — building and planting, livestock and treasure and hearing songs — and there is no mention of women. And the commentators disagreed about the word שדה, and the best of all is that it is from שדד, women taken by force in plunder and captivity, that he chooses from among them according to his desire. And the matter of שדה ושדות — one and many, like <i>רחם רחמתים</i> (Ecclesiastes 4:2): for the head of a man, possessor of רחם — one woman or two; and the meaning is that you should not say one alone, for there is one who seizes two."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra cites the phrase רחם רחמתים from Ecclesiastes 4:2 (רחם in construct before a noun is pausal form רחמתים); rendered hyper-literally without expanding his compressed grammatical argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:01.350387530Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}